{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI have been in the Emperor’s greenhouses by the Burg. It is a remarkable place, though the air is close and heavy, quite unlike the crisp evening here. I entered and left through an underground passage that the Emperor uses daily for his afternoon walks. It struck me as a curious little mechanism of power: the sovereign moving through the earth, hidden from the world, while his subjects gaze at the leaves above. It is a physical symbol of how the state operates—often unseen, yet structuring everything we see.\n\nI am tired now, but my spirits are good. The light in this city has a particular quality tonight; it feels less like the grey fog of Berlin and more like a promise. I think of you and the boys, and how strange it is to be so far from the familiar. I will rest soon, but I shall write again when we move on.\n\nYour affectionate husband,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795219126,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":199,"prompt_tokens":900,"total_tokens":1099,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-nAdDVNbk0Pd4VFPcDBvOeSlbY0NKNgrX","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":900,"prompt_ms":886.109,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9845655555555556,"prompt_per_second":1015.676400984529,"predicted_n":199,"predicted_ms":4731.214,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.895020202020202,"predicted_per_second":41.849723982047735}}